        "original_id": "43771ac9-4c57-5095-aaac-852a20bc4357",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Randall Park, Seth Rogen, Evan Goldberg, Kim Jong-Un, Danny Chung, Eddie Huang, Louis Huang\n- Works: The Interview, Veep, Fresh Off the Boat, Vice documentary\n- Roles: actor, comedian, writer, director, governor, restaurateur\n\nFacts:\n- Randall Park was born on March 23, 1974, and he is an American actor, comedian, writer, and director.\n- A Vice documentary that was shot in 2012 heavily inspired the 2014 film The Interview.\n- The Interview is a 2014 American action comedy film directed by Seth Rogen and Evan Goldberg.\n- In 2014, Randall Park played Kim Jong-Un in the film The Interview.\n- Beginning in 2015, Randall Park portrayed Louis Huang, Eddie Huang's father and an American restaurateur, in ABC's television show Fresh Off the Boat.\n- Randall Park played Minnesota governor Danny Chung in Veep.",
